funes.cpp change log
====================

0.2.0  (2026-04-21)
-------------------

  * Bump LogosDB to v0.3.2 for cross-platform support (Windows, Linux, macOS).
    - Windows support via platform-compatible memory mapping
    - Batch put: ~4× faster for bulk ingestion (30K vectors/sec vs 7.5K)
    - Delete/update operations available
    - New APIs: logosdb_put_batch(), logosdb_delete(), logosdb_update()

0.1.1  (2025-06-25)
-------------------

  * Replace atoi with strtol + range validation for all --semantic-memory-* numeric flags.
  * Document all CLI flags in SPECS.md (11 previously undocumented flags added).
  * Add LFM (Liquid AI) to supported architecture list.

0.1.0  (2025-06-25)
-------------------

  Initial release.

  * Semantic memory via context-window injection (Quote/Hint).
  * LogosDB v0.1.0 as storage backend (HNSW search, mmap vectors, JSONL metadata).
  * Dual injection: LLM compressor chooses Quote (literal) or Hint (summary).
  * Heuristic keyword hint fallback when LLM compress is off.
  * Temporal context: pre-computed date arithmetic injected into compressor prompt.
  * Teach via /teach command, <teach> tags, teach prefix, and learn-from-response.
  * Teach variants (paraphrase generation) for robust recall.
  * Model-agnostic: works with all 100+ architectures supported by llama.cpp.
  * Tested with LLaMA, Qwen, Gemma, Phi, Mistral, DeepSeek, Command-R,
    GPT-2/NeoX, Falcon, LFM (Liquid), and Mamba families.
  * Removed experimental latent hidden-state injection (no benchmark lift).
  * Removed logit-bias injection path.
  * Single executable (llama-cli) with LogosDB statically linked.
